Tarantool is an in-memory computing platform consisting of a database
and an application server.

Key features of the application server:

- A heavily optimized Lua interpreter with a fast tracing JIT compiler,
  based on LuaJIT 2.1.
- Cooperative multitasking and non-blocking IO.
- Persistent queues, sharding and a cluster/application management
  framework.
- Access to external databases such as MySQL and PostgreSQL.
- A rich set of built-in and standalone modules.

Key features of the database:

- MessagePack data format and a MessagePack based client-server protocol.
- Two data engines: a 100% in-memory one with complete WAL-based
  persistence and an LSM-tree based one for large data sets.
- Multiple index types: HASH, TREE, RTREE, BITSET.
- Document oriented JSON path indexes.
- Asynchronous master-master and synchronous quorum-based replication.
- RAFT-based automatic leader election for single-leader configurations.
- Authentication and access control.
- ANSI SQL, including views, joins, referential and check constraints.
- Connectors for many programming languages.

The database is a C extension of the application server and can be
turned off.
